 HISTORY                                                          8099 1451
 -------                                                          8099 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  8099 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The        8099 1451
 thermal scattering law data for uranium metal was developed      8099 1451
 using molecular dynamics (MD) with lattice dynamics [1]. The     8099 1451
 coherent elastic cross sections were calculated based on the     8099 1451
 experimental lattice constants. Free atom cross sections were    8099 1451
 taken from ENDF/B-VIII.0 nuclide evaluations at 1e-5 eV [2].     8099 1451
 Seven temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law   8099 1451
 Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to       8099 1451
 produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for U-metal [3]. The coherent      8099 1451
 elastic data were prepared using the cubic approximation.        8099 1451
 MAT=8099 and ZA=8199 are used for U-metal (HEU - 93% enriched).  8099 1451
